{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Recurrence 2026-10-19 ~03:25 PDT: a `review_plan_start` on ed5a-3042-e4e0-45c1 completed but `gate_status.durable` reads `stale-store`: \"the local ticket store holds 6 committed ticket event(s) the shared store has never received (last delivery failure: final-push-rejected)\". Same mechanism as yesterday's fork, now in its PUSH_PENDING form: three lanes landed three changes within ~40 min (b1228deb72f, 441ca94f4a8, 5ad259f2c75) with their local-CLI closes and compactions writing to `origin/tickets` at a rate the server's fetch-merge-push cycle loses to, and `final-push-rejected` means the five recovery cycles were exhausted on one write. Only one MCP container is running (no autodeploy overlap this time), so this is the write-rate half of the cause on its own. This comment is itself the ordinary MCP write that restarted recovery yesterday; if `plan_review_status` reads `certified` again within a few minutes, AC6's idle-time sync plus a larger or adaptive retry budget is the fix; if not, the server needs the operator push."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792408335336381714,"uuid":"516b15a7-eacd-4eb5-8471-a11bac793ca2"}